From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] Assign handles for fences, semaphores, pipelines and
 object arrays

Fences and semaphores use guest-assigned handles when bit 0x80 is agreed; a
fence created signaled is known signaled without asking the device. Pipeline
creates assign one handle per pipeline unless a create info sets
FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED, whose result must be waited for. With bit
0x100, descriptor set and command buffer allocations assign their handles too.
Handles are minted in consecutive blocks under a 24-bit tag; a process that
exhausts a tag's 32-bit counter continues under a fresh tag, so no handle is
ever handed out twice. Array creates defer one reply of all handles and a
result.
